SIGN-OFF REQUIREMENT

All commits must be signed off by the author using `git commit -s`, which
automatically appends a "Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>"
trailer to your commit message. This sign-off is our way of tracking
contribution provenance and ensuring legal accountability. It certifies
that you have written the code and have the right to contribute it to
the project under the applicable open source license (see LICENSE).

Example:
  $ git commit -s -m "Your commit message here"

This will append the Signed-off-by line with your git user name and email
(configured via `git config user.name` and `git config user.email`).
